From: Ghaf contributors <ghaf@tii.ae>
Subject: [PATCH] tegra/fbdev: take the core-allocated fb_info on Linux >= 6.12.103

Linux 63c971af4036 ("drm/fb-helper: Allocate and release fb_info in single
place"), backported into stable 6.12.103, deleted both
drm_fb_helper_alloc_info() and drm_fb_helper_release_info() from
include/drm/drm_fb_helper.h. The core now allocates fb_helper->info before it
calls the driver's fbdev probe.

That breaks nvidia-oot's conftest ladder here: NV_DRM_FB_HELPER_ALLOC_INFO_PRESENT
stops matching, so the build falls through to drm_fb_helper_alloc_fbi(), gone
since v6.2, and the module fails to compile with

  fbdev.c:128:16: error: implicit declaration of function 'drm_fb_helper_alloc_fbi'

Ghaf hits this because the passthrough guests build these out-of-tree modules
against a mainline kernel (boot.kernelPackages = pkgs.linuxPackages_6_12 in
../payload/guest-module.nix), not against the L4T 5.15 kernel jetpack itself
uses -- so jetpack-nixos has no reason to have fixed it upstream yet.

Add the missing branch, mirroring what the in-tree tegra driver does after the
same commit (see also d23bd83f3e47, "drm/tegra: fbdev: Do not assign to struct
drm_fb_helper.info"): use the fb_info the core already allocated. The later
`helper->info = info` assignment becomes a self-assignment; it is left alone to
keep this to one hunk.

Drop this patch once jetpack-nixos ships an nvidia-oot that knows about the new
fb-helper contract.
---
diff --git a/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/fbdev.c b/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/fbdev.c
--- a/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/fbdev.c
+++ b/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/fbdev.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <nvidia/conftest.h>
 
 #include <linux/console.h>
+#include <linux/version.h>
 #include <linux/vmalloc.h>
 
 #include <drm/drm_drv.h>
@@ -124,6 +125,16 @@
 
 #if defined(NV_DRM_FB_HELPER_ALLOC_INFO_PRESENT) /* Linux v6.2 */
 	info = drm_fb_helper_alloc_info(helper);
+#elif LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 12, 103)
+	/*
+	 * Linux 63c971af4036 ("drm/fb-helper: Allocate and release fb_info in
+	 * single place"), backported to 6.12.103, removed both
+	 * drm_fb_helper_alloc_info() and drm_fb_helper_release_info(); the core
+	 * allocates helper->info before it calls the fbdev probe. The conftest
+	 * above fails on such a kernel and the pre-v6.2 fallback below is long
+	 * gone, so take the fb_info the core allocated for us.
+	 */
+	info = helper->info;
 #else
 	info = drm_fb_helper_alloc_fbi(helper);
 #endif
